# 5) Users and roles\
- **Manager / Leader (builder and pusher):**  \
  - Can create **Module core (opus)** from a prompt or from uploads/links.  \
  - Refines the core by adding, removing, and adjusting.  \
  - Defines and pushes **lesson streams** generated from the core to teams and tracks progress.  \
  - Locks the **Module core** as \'91Company Module\'92 in the client\'92s **Content Library (Client Library)**. Only owners and client admins can edit.  \
  - Cannot edit the **Certified Core**, but can add a clearly labelled local wrap (intro, examples, rules).\
- **Learner (team member):**  \
  - Receives short items in Slack, Teams, or web.  \
  - Interacts in natural language: answer items, ask for help, challenge content, or ask \'93How am I doing?\'94 to get progress.  \
  - Gets instant feedback and varied practice.  \
  - Never sees the exact same item twice unless the module is tagged **Compliance Critical**.\
- **Certifier (named expert):**  \
  - Reviews and stamps **Module core** for the Certified catalogue.  \
  - Can start from a prompt or from uploads.  \
  - Locks content as **Certified Candidate**, which after review becomes **Certified Core** (read\uc0\u8209 only for clients).\
- **Consultant (Cerply or partner):**  \
  - Helps set up, drafts **Module core** from prompts or uploads, and saves drafts to the client\'92s **Content Library (Client Library)**.  \
  - May **propose lock** as Company Module; a **Manager must approve/certify** before it becomes locked; ownership then moves to a client admin; consultant keeps read\uc0\u8209 only history.\
- **Company owner (client admin):** sets up teams, rights, rules, and data controls.  \
- **Cerply owner (platform admin):** manages catalogue, pricing, rights, and safety.\
\
