# 8) End\uc0\u8209 to\u8209 end flows\
## 8.1 Build flow (manager/leader)\
1) Open the Build workspace with three panes: **Chat**, **Content**, **Calibration**.  \
2) In **Chat**, you can start with a plain prompt (for example: \'93Create a week\uc0\u8209 one onboarding module for trade capture analysts. Include two quick checks per lesson.\'94) and/or upload files and links.  \
3) Agent proposes an outline and a short plan. Accept or edit.  \
4) Agent drafts the **Module core** (sections, key points, citations) in **Content**, then generates lessons and quizzes from that core.  \
5) Manager edits in **Content** and presses **Send**; while the agent is writing, **Content** is locked to avoid clashes.  \
6) **Calibration** shows example lessons and quizzes at varied difficulty with reasons. Tap **Add to chat** to steer tone and level.  \
7) When ready, **Lock** the Module core by role: Company Module (manager approval required if created by a consultant) or Certified Candidate. Consultants save drafts to the client\'92s **Content Library** and may propose lock.\
\
## 8.2 Push flow (to learners)\
1) Choose a **Module**, then choose or define a **lesson stream** derived from the core, and select the audience (teams, groups, or named people).  \
2) Choose when to send (now, schedule).  \
3) Learners receive prompts in Slack, Teams, or on the web.  \
4) The engine adapts each item based on past answers, speed, signs of doubt, and time since last practice. Content is varied so it is not a repeat (exact repeats are allowed only if the module is tagged **Compliance Critical**).  \
5) Gentle reminders and light rewards keep the habit.  \
6) Prompts limited to 1\'962 per day mandatory; learners can choose to continue learning beyond the cap.  \
7) **Quiet hours default**: 20:00\'9608:00 local time (timezone\uc0\u8209 adaptive). Managers can override.\
8) Groups and audiences are created and managed in Cerply at first; we can accommodate client directory sync as needed.\
\
## 8.3 Learn flow (learner)\
1) Learner gets a short nudge with a single task.  \
2) Interact in natural language to answer, ask for help, or challenge content.  \
3) Ask \'93How am I doing?\'94 to receive a compact progress card with **current level**, **streak**, **next due**, and actions **Continue** / **Review weak area**.  \
4) Next item adjusts in level and shape (for example, from recall to a short case).  \
5) A quick recap is available on request.  \
6) The engine plans the next session time to strengthen memory.\
\
## 8.4 Track flow (manager/leader)\
1) Open a dashboard for a team or a person.  \
2) See progress against skills, time to first competence, recent activity, and stuck areas.  \
3) Drill into a module to see which parts work and which are stale.  \
4) Export a PDF of a complete module for review with watermark and version stamp; no learner exports.\
\
## 8.5 Certified flow (expert and admin)\
1) Submit a module for review with sources and tags.  \
2) Reviewer checks clarity, accuracy, and sample items.  \
3) Reviewer stamps it and adds tags, sector, and level.  \
4) Module goes into the Certified catalogue.  \
5) Client managers can push **lesson streams generated from Certified Core** and add a local wrap.  \
6) Client wraps must be **clearly labelled** (e.g., \'93Client Addendum\'94) and must not change the Certified Core goals.  \
7) Version history tracks who changed what and when.  \
8) **Example\uc0\u8209 only SLAs:** urgent takedown within 24 hours; standard review within 5 business days.\
