# 9) Functional requirements\
## 9.1 Build workspace (three panes)\
**Chat pane**  \
- Free\uc0\u8209 text prompts and quick starters (for example, \'93build onboarding from these files\'94).  \
- File and link upload.  \
- Show the agent\'92s plan before big changes.  \
- Full change log with who said what and when.  \
- **Prompt\uc0\u8209 to\u8209 Module** button that seeds a clean outline from a plain brief.\
\
**Content pane**  \
- Live draft of the **Module core** (sections, key points, source map) **and** generated lessons/checks, goals, and tags.  \
- Manager edits are applied on **Send**.  \
- Pane locks while the agent writes.  \
- Warn on conflicts with newer agent changes.  \
- Save to the client **Content Library (Client Library)**.  \
- Submit for stamp to Certified review.  \
- Certified Core is read\uc0\u8209 only; clients can add a local wrap without changing the core.\
\
**Calibration pane**  \
- Shows example items at several levels of challenge, with reasons.  \
- One\uc0\u8209 click **Add to chat** to request a change.\
\
**Done when**  \
- A manager can create a ready module from a prompt alone, or a mix of prompt and uploads, in one sitting without help.\
\
## 9.2 Content model\
- A **Module core** has: title, goals, **sections**, **source map/citations**, target roles, tags (including flags like **Compliance Critical**), sector, version, owner, visibility (private / company / Certified).  \
- **Derived assets:**  \
  - **Lesson streams** \'97 scheduled sequences of short lessons and quick checks generated from the core for a chosen audience.  \
  - **Quick checks** \'97 single task items (for example, short question) linked back to core sections and goals.  \
  - **Guidance notes** \'97 short practical notes or SOPs extracted from the core.  \
- **Item types:** choice, short text, arrange steps, label parts, short case, or \'93do then reflect\'94.  \
- **Linkage:** every item links to one or more core sections and goals, and stores the **core version** it was generated from.  \
- **Versioning:** all parts are versioned; regenerating items from a new core version records lineage.\
\
## 9.3 Agent and tools (prompt\uc0\u8209 to\u8209 module and role\u8209 based locking)\
**Purpose**  \
Let builders create new content from a plain prompt, not just uploads. Managers, Certifiers, and Consultants can ask the agent to draft, then refine until it is right. When done, they lock it as theirs (with rules by role).\
\
**Sources the agent may use (set per client):**  \
- Cerply Certified catalogue (read\uc0\u8209 only).  \
- Cerply public library (read/write for patterns and templates).  \
- Client private library (read/write \'97 client\'92s content and team details).  \
- The open web (read\uc0\u8209 only; **default ON**, controlled by client content rules and filter lists).\
\
**Draft loop:**  \
1) Agent proposes an outline and a short plan.  \
2) Builder accepts or edits the outline.  \
3) Agent drafts the **Module core** (sections, key points, citations) and then generates lessons and quick checks from that core with sources and notes.  \
4) Builder edits in **Content** or asks for changes in **Chat**.  \
5) **Calibration** shows examples at varied difficulty; builder can \'93add to chat\'94 to steer tone and level.  \
6) Agent flags gaps and suggests items to add or remove.\
\
**Quality gates before lock:**  \
- Citations present and check out.  \
- No obvious errors or made\uc0\u8209 up facts.  \
- Reading level and length match the target role.  \
- Duplicates removed; items are varied.  \
- Basic accessibility checks passed.\
\
**Role\uc0\u8209 based ownership and locking**  \
- **Manager / Leader:** **Lock as Company Module** in the client\'92s **Content Library (Client Library)**. Others can clone; only owners and client admins can edit. Locking creates an immutable version; later edits create a new version.  \
- **Certifier:** **Lock as Certified Candidate** which enters the review flow. After stamp, it becomes **Certified Core** (read\uc0\u8209 only) that clients can push and wrap.  \
- **Consultant:** save drafts to the client\'92s **Content Library** and **propose** lock as Company Module; **manager approval/certification is required** for lock. After approval, ownership moves to a client admin; the consultant keeps a read\uc0\u8209 only copy in their work history.\
\
**Fork and merge**  \
- Anyone with access can clone a module; the system keeps lineage to the parent.  \
- Change requests can be proposed back to the owner for review and merge.\
\
**Models and tools policy**  \
- Default drafting uses a fast, low\uc0\u8209 cost model (for example, Anthropic Haiku or GPT\u8209 5 mini).  \
- First\uc0\u8209 pass content with citations can call **GPT\u8209 5 Pro**.  \
- Fact and citation checks can call **Claude Sonnet 4.5**.  \
- The agent can call: Adaptive Engine (to shape examples), Cerply stores, client store, Certified catalogue, and the open web (if allowed).  \
- The agent logs all sources and tools used for each draft.\
\
**Usage rights**  \
- Client owns **Company Modules** in their **Content Library (Client Library)**.  \
- Cerply owns the platform and shared templates.  \
- **Certified Core** follows the Certified licence; experts are credited; any revenue share rules are recorded.\
\
**Done when**  \
- A builder can create a full module with no prior uploads using only prompts and allowed sources, pass quality gates, and lock it within one hour.\
\
## 9.4 Push to channels\
- Send to Slack, Teams, and the Cerply web app.  \
- Target by team, group, or named people.  \
- Send now or schedule.  \
- Set **mandatory** or **recommended**.  \
- Set pace rules (for example, \'93proficient within 1 month\'94).  \
- Nudge rules (for example, gentle reminder after two days idle for mandatory modules).  \
- **Quiet hours default**: 20:00\'9608:00 local time (timezone\uc0\u8209 adaptive); managers can override.  \
- Each send creates unique variants **derived from the Module core** so exact repeats are rare (allowed only for **Compliance Critical**).\
- Learners can mute a module and unmute later (if recommended, not mandatory).  \
- Groups are managed inside Cerply at first; we can accommodate client directory sync.\
\
**Done when**  \
- A manager can send a module to a team and see delivery stats within minutes.\
\
## 9.5 Adaptive Learning Engine\
- Actively borrows from current research and proven methods.  \
- Stores every learner action unless the client asks us to remove it; when removals happen, we retain anonymous patterns/aggregates for long\uc0\u8209 term optimisation.  \
- Adjusts item level based on past correctness, speed, signs of doubt, and time since last practice.  \
- Mixes item shapes to keep interest.  \
- Plans the next session time to build long\uc0\u8209 term memory.  \
- Detects weak areas and brings them back at the right time.  \
- Flags stale items for the manager to refresh, based on learner feedback, external triggers, or time since last refresh/recert.  \
- Prioritises recent, weak, or urgent topics over modules in which the learner shows high proficiency.  \
\
**Done when**  \
- Learners show steady gains in target skills; exact repeats occur only in modules tagged **Compliance Critical**.\
\
## 9.6 Tracking and dashboards\
- **Team view:** mastery by skill, time to first competence, active users, at\uc0\u8209 risk users, recent wins, stale modules.  \
- **Person view:** current level, pace, weak areas, streaks, and last session time.  \
- **Module view:** **core freshness (stale sections), version age**, reach and answer rates across **derived lesson streams**, time on task, drop\uc0\u8209 offs, items that confuse, items that are too easy.  \
- Filters by team, role, date, module, and skill.  \
- **Exports:** Managers/Certifiers/Admin can export **complete modules as PDF** for review **with watermark and version stamp**; no exports for learners.\
\
**Done when**  \
- A leader can open one page and know who needs help and which module needs work.\
\
## 9.7 Certified catalogue\
- Submit for review with sources and tags.  \
- Reviewer checklist: clarity, accuracy, relevance, sector fit.  \
- Stamp with expert name and profile.  \
- Versioning and change log.  \
- Search and filter by skill, sector, level, role.  \
- Usage rights: clients can push and wrap; cannot edit core.  \
- **Client wraps must be clearly labelled** (e.g., \'93Client Addendum\'94) and must not change Certified Core goals.  \
- Takedown flow for errors or legal issues.  \
- **Example\uc0\u8209 only SLAs:** urgent takedown within 24 hours; standard review within 5 business days.\
\
**Done when**  \
- Managers can find, trust, and use a stamped module the same day.\
\
## 9.8 Admin and governance\
- Company set\uc0\u8209 up, teams, roles; **invite links at launch** (single sign\u8209 on to follow as client demand requires).  \
- Rights: who can build, push, track, submit, review, stamp.  \
- Audit log for important actions.  \
- Data controls: region choice, export, delete on request.  \
- Branded theme per client.\
